{"content":[{"c":["YOKE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The wooden bar that allowed two (or more) draft animals to be coupled (yoked) so that they might effectively work together (",{"href":"?bref=Num.19.2","r":"Num.19.2","rawR":"Num.19.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.19.2","value":"Num.19.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 19:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.19","r":"1Kgs.19.19","rawR":"1Kgs.19.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.19","value":"1Kgs.19.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.3","r":"Job.1.3","rawR":"Job.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.3","value":"Job.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 1:3"},"). In addition to this literal usage, the Bible frequently uses the term metaphorically to refer to work or bondage (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.26.13","r":"Lev.26.13","rawR":"Lev.26.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.26.13","value":"Lev.26.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 26:13"},"). The yoke of bondage was applied not only by foreign oppressors but often by Israel’s own kings as well (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.4-14","r":"1Kgs.12.4-14","rawR":"1Kgs.12.4-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.4-14","value":"1Kgs.12.4-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 12:4-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.10.4-14","r":"2Chr.10.4-14","rawR":"2Chr.10.4-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.10.4-14","value":"2Chr.10.4-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 10:4-14"},"). In prophetic writings, the yoke of bondage was generally associated with divine judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Lam.1.14","r":"Lam.1.14","rawR":"Lam.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lam.1.14","value":"Lam.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lam 1:14"},"), so that deliverance was represented as God breaking the yoke that had enslaved Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.9.4","r":"Isa.9.4","rawR":"Isa.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.9.4","value":"Isa.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 9:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.10.27","r":"Isa.10.27","rawR":"Isa.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.10.27","value":"Isa.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.14.25","r":"Isa.14.25","rawR":"Isa.14.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.14.25","value":"Isa.14.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.58.6","r":"Isa.58.6","rawR":"Isa.58.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.58.6","value":"Isa.58.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"58:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.2.20","r":"Jer.2.20","rawR":"Jer.2.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.2.20","value":"Jer.2.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 2:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.5.5","r":"Jer.5.5","rawR":"Jer.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.5.5","value":"Jer.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:5"},"). The yoke of bondage figured prominently in Jeremiah’s dispute with Hananiah’s prophecy concerning Judah’s imminent release from Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.27.8-11","r":"Jer.27.8-11","rawR":"Jer.27.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.27.8-11","value":"Jer.27.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 27:8-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.28.1-17","r":"Jer.28.1-17","rawR":"Jer.28.1-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.28.1-17","value":"Jer.28.1-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:1-17"},"). In the NT, Jesus transforms “yoke” into a positive term by calling on people to take up his yoke, which is not burdensome, and he will give them rest for their souls (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.11.29-30","r":"Matt.11.29-30","rawR":"Matt.11.29-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.11.29-30","value":"Matt.11.29-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 11:29-30"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Yoke","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 19:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.19.2","rawQueryValue":"Num.19.2","sourceRefExact":"Num.19.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 19:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.19.19","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.19.19","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.19.19"},{"anchorText":"Jb 1:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.1.3","rawQueryValue":"Job.1.3","sourceRefExact":"Job.1.3"},{"anchorText":"Lv 26:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.26.13","rawQueryValue":"Lev.26.13","sourceRefExact":"Lev.26.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 12:4-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.12.4-14","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.12.4-14","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.12.4-14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 10:4-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.10.4-14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.10.4-14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.10.4-14"},{"anchorText":"Lam 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lam.1.14","rawQueryValue":"Lam.1.14","sourceRefExact":"Lam.1.14"},{"anchorText":"Is 9:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.9.4","rawQueryValue":"Isa.9.4","sourceRefExact":"Isa.9.4"},{"anchorText":"10:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.10.27","rawQueryValue":"Isa.10.27","sourceRefExact":"Isa.10.27"},{"anchorText":"14:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.14.25","rawQueryValue":"Isa.14.25","sourceRefExact":"Isa.14.25"},{"anchorText":"58:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.58.6","rawQueryValue":"Isa.58.6","sourceRefExact":"Isa.58.6"},{"anchorText":"Jer 2:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.2.20","rawQueryValue":"Jer.2.20","sourceRefExact":"Jer.2.20"},{"anchorText":"5:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.5.5","rawQueryValue":"Jer.5.5","sourceRefExact":"Jer.5.5"},{"anchorText":"Jer 27:8-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.27.8-11","rawQueryValue":"Jer.27.8-11","sourceRefExact":"Jer.27.8-11"},{"anchorText":"28:1-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.28.1-17","rawQueryValue":"Jer.28.1-17","sourceRefExact":"Jer.28.1-17"},{"anchorText":"Mt 11:29-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.11.29-30","rawQueryValue":"Matt.11.29-30","sourceRefExact":"Matt.11.29-30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"94bbebf07272fc1289198d9bc4bf4d7004462ec2cd7ac53150e490f15e7cbebb","sourceItemName":"Yoke","sourceItemOrder":9,"sourceMember":"Articles/XY.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"PairsOfOxenLinkedWithYokes","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Yoke","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Yoke","title":"Yoke","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}